    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it's green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `riskFlag` on the owner response, true when any of: the owner is a possible duplicate, the email domain is disposable-adjacent, or the city is over its soft capacity.\n\n**Changes (3 files):**\n\n1. **`RiskFlag.java`** (new, self-contained helper in the owner function package) \u2014 a single public `of(owner, repository)` that ORs three small private checks. It recomputes from persisted state (the create-time flags are `@Transient` and lost on reload), so the value is consistent on both the `POST` create response and the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read-back the test uses. Each check reuses existing logic:\n   - *possible duplicate* mirrors `FlagPossibleDuplicate` (same postcode + phonetic surname, different identity key, not the same household);\n   - *disposable-adjacent* flags an email whose second-level label matches one of `CheckEmailDomain`'s blocked providers regardless of TLD (a softer notion than the exact-match block, which rejects at create time);\n   - *over soft capacity* reuses `CheckCityCapacity.normalize` and `FlagCapacityWarning.WARN_THRESHOLD` (40).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating `riskFlag` to `RiskFlag.of(owner, ownerRepository)` (the mapper already autowires `ownerRepository`).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` read-only boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n**Structural impact kept low:** the only existing *function* changed is the abstract `toOwnerDto` (one annotation line, CC 1); all new behaviour lives in a fresh cohesive class with no surrounding-class complexity to hold.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (the only test class) passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. A normal unique owner (no email, unique city/surname) yields `riskFlag=false` as the test asserts.",
